# Dense reader, written in A0 (Stages A, B1, B2 and B3.1). The dense text of one file becomes the canonical
# text of its program: src/dense.ts parseDense, then formatProgram. Stage A covers the forms that
# the corpus fixtures and examples/kernels.a0 use, and records: explicit ids and
# the default names a, b, ... of nodes that have none; nesting (a value used once is written in
# its consumer, as in `add mul A B C`); records (`(a b)`, `(x,)`, and `(x)` for x); at and put on
# records; parameters A, B, ... and pN; u32 and bool literals; the arithmetic, comparison and
# select operations and mov; use lines (skipped: the canonical text has none); function headers
# with u32, bool or record types, and the first statement on the header line.
# Stage B1 adds calls: `g A B` (a first word or an identifier that names a function) and
# `call g A B`, of a function defined earlier in the same input. The arity of the callee is the
# type count of its header or, for a header without types, one more than the highest parameter its
# nodes and result use; a callee that is later, the function itself or in a used file, a wrong
# operand count, and an overflow set the error flag. Arguments of a call are kept in a pool.
# Stage B2 adds fold and loop: `fold F n s a..` and `loop P F n s a..`, where F and P are the names
# of functions defined earlier, or inline bodies `{statement; statement}` (the last statement is the
# result). The operand count is the arity of the body F (of P when F is inline; the larger of the
# two when both are inline); an inline body has the parameters A (the state), B (the step) and C...
# (the extra operands), at least 2. Each inline body is lifted: it becomes the function CALLER_N, N
# counting the bodies of the function CALLER in the order its fold and loop nodes complete (a
# predicate before its body), written before CALLER with the signature the reference reader derives
# (the state type of the initial value, u32, the types of the extra operands; bool, or the state type,
# as the result). A state or extra operand of an inline body that is not u32 or bool sets the error
# flag. The result of a function with no `->` is what the reference reader infers: u32 when the
# result value is u32 or has no type, bool when it is a bool. The reader also refuses what the
# reference rejects and the earlier stages read: a function name that is a keyword or not an
# identifier, a type that is not u32, bool or a record of them, a name written twice, anything
# after a `ret` statement of a function, a function with no statement.
# Stage B3.1 adds arrays: the types u32xN, boolxN and their dimensions (u32x128x16 is 16 arrays of 128 u32),
# also after a record ((u32,u32)x128x32), in a header (the lexer checks a type word, tvtok the whole type and
# its width of at most 2097152 bits), the literal `[a b c]`, and the operations get (2 operands) and set (3).
# The mask of a node (see below) tells an array of u32 or bool of one or two dimensions from any other type
# (get and set of it are typed; any other array is the mask 8, and its get is any type), so a function whose
# result is not written and ends in an array, or in a value of an unknown type, sets the error flag.
# Stage B3.2 adds the repeat form `[x;n]` (n copies of the first element; elements may follow it, as in the
# reference), the escape `$name` (the lexer reads it as the word `name` with the flag 128, so the reader
# takes it for a name of a node defined above, or for the name of a statement, never a keyword or a function),
# and `=` after the name of a statement.
# Not yet read (the error flag is set): text, io, spec lines, hex
# literals, profile lines, commas used as blanks, the `rec` and `arr` words, record and array states and
# extra operands of inline bodies, and records and arrays as an unwritten result.
#
# Input: the dense bytes src[0..n) as 128-byte pages (n <= 16384). Output: the canonical bytes as
# pages of 128 (at most 16384 bytes) and the error flag, set when the input or the output is over
# a capacity (16384 bytes, 4096 tokens, 2048 lines, 2048 nodes, 1024 nodes of inline bodies, 512
# inline bodies, 512 functions, 2048 parameters, 8 nested frames, 3072 call arguments, 2944 array
# elements: 2112 in the arrays at the first level, 448 at the second, 64 at each of the next six) or a
# construct is outside the forms above. The name and id tables of a function
# hold 2048 entries, the node capacity, so every node of an accepted program has its own entry.
# Every pass is a fold over paged tables; there is no control flow, so every branch is a select,
# and a fold with a count of 0 does nothing.
#
# Passes:
#   0 fnscan: each line that starts with `fn` names a function; the name tokens seed the function
#     table and their count the meta entry of the node table, so a word is a function name before
#     (or without) the function being read; a name defined twice is an error.
#   1 lexb: each byte (and a virtual newline at n) appends its word and punctuation tokens and
#     the line boundaries (the token count at each newline) to paged tables.
#   2 lines: each line is a function header (`fn NAME [TYPES ->] [RESULT]`, the rest of the
#     line its first statement) or a statement; statements are prefix expressions, parsed
#     forward with a frame stack, so a node is created after its operands (canonical order). The
#     inline bodies of a statement are read first (prestep, bodyrun): the statements of each
#     become nodes of the body region, and its descriptor is kept; the fold or loop word takes the
#     next descriptor, skips the body tokens, and its node completes like a call.
#   3 print: each function as its canonical lines, its lifted bodies first; default names are the
#     candidates a..zzzz that are neither keywords nor explicit names, in node order.
#
# Token: (kind, len, start, w0, w1, hh, nv, fl). kind 1 word, 3 ( 4 ) 5 [ 6 ] 7 , 8 quote, 9 error
# byte, 10 ; 11 { 12 }.
# w0 and w1 pack the first 8 bytes (big-endian, no padding), hh is a hash of all bytes, nv the
# value of a number (or of the parameter letter or pN, or the mask of a type word), fl bit 0 digits, bit 1 pN,
# bit 2 A-Z, bit 3 a word of the form of a type (u32, bool or io, then dimensions x4x2: never an id), bit 4 such
# a word that is a valid type, bit 5 a valid run of dimensions (x4x2, after a record), bit 6 `io`; bits 8..
# the width in bits of the type, or the product of the dimensions, saturated just over 4194304.
# Node: (op, idt, nargs, k0, v0, k1, v1, k2, v2, k3, v3); idt 0 default name, 1+token for an
# explicit name, 4294967295 the fresh `retval`. Operand kinds: 1 node, 2 parameter, 3 u32, 4 bool.
# The node table has 40 pages of 128 entries: nodes 0..2047, the meta entry 2048 (field 3 the next
# free pool argument, 5 the function count, 6 the inline bodies lifted so far in the function, 7 the
# descriptors so far, 8 the body nodes so far), the call-argument pool 2049..2816 (four operands to an entry, in
# the fields of k0..v3: 3072 arguments), the elements of the array literals as the arguments 3072.. (entries
# 2817..3552: a region for the frame at each depth, so that the elements of a literal stay together while
# literals nest: arguments 3072..5183, 5184..5631, then 64 each from 5632), 3553 a dummy write target, 3554
# the next free place of each region (fields 0..7), the nodes of the inline bodies 3555..4578, and the
# descriptors of the inline bodies 4579..5090 (first node, node count, result
# kind, result value, parameter count). An array literal is a node (op 27) with k1 and v1 as a call has
# them, k2 = 6 and v2 the first of its nargs elements; its frame (op 27, never full) writes each element to
# the next place of its region and `]` makes the node. A call node (op 24) has k0 = 5 and
# v0 the callee, k1 = 2 and v1 the highest parameter its arguments use (or k1 = 0), k2 = 6 and v2
# the pool index of its first argument; nargs is the arity. A call frame (op 24) keeps the same
# k0, v0, k2, v2 and writes each argument to the pool as it completes. A fold node (op 25) and a
# loop node (op 26) are the same, with k0 = 5 and v0 the body function (k0 = 7 and v0 the
# descriptor of an inline body), and for a loop k3 and v3 the predicate in the same way; k2 is 6 plus
# 8 times the number of bodies lifted before the node, which numbers its inline bodies.
# A type is a mask of what it can be: 1 u32, 2 bool, 4 an error (the reference reader gives no type),
# 8 another type, or a descriptor of an array of u32 or bool of one or two dimensions: 8 + 16 + 32 if
# bool + 64 if two dimensions + 128 times the length less one of the first dimension (of 16 bits, or of
# 12 bits when there are two) + 524288 times the length less one of the second. The result mask of each
# function is kept in field 8 of its function table entry.

fn ztok -> (u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32)x128x32
zr rec 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
zp arr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr zr
zt arr zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp
ret zt
end

fn zlnt -> u32x128x16
zu mov 0
zp arr zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu zu
zt arr zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp zp
ret zt
end

fn s1zero -> ((u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32)x128x32,u32,u32x128x16,u32,bool,bool,bool,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,bool,bool,bool,u32,bool,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,bool)
tk0 call ztok
bd0 call zlnt
r rec tk0 0 bd0 0 false false false 0 0 0 0 0 0 false false false 0 false 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 false
ret r
end

fn tokput (u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32)x128x32 u32 (u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32) -> (u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32)x128x32
ix shr p1 7
pg get p0 ix
lo and p1 127
pg2 set pg lo p2
r set p0 ix pg2
ret r
end

fn bput u32x128x16 u32 u32 -> u32x128x16
ix shr p1 7
pg get p0 ix
lo and p1 127
pg2 set pg lo p2
r set p0 ix pg2
ret r
end

# The product of two sizes, saturated: anything over 4194304 is 4194305.
fn satm u32 u32 -> u32
z eq p1 0
bz select z 1 p1
lim div 4194304 bz
big gt p0 lim
pr mul p0 p1
r select big 4194305 pr
ret r
end

