# One token of a type (a run of glued tokens): the state (depth of parentheses, 1 when a type has just
# ended, still valid, the width in bits of the last item, the widths of the open records by depth). A type
# is u32, bool, an array of them (u32x4, boolx2x3: the lexer checks the word), or a record: parentheses around
# types separated by commas, each followed by array dimensions as one glued word (x4x2). The width of a
# value is at most 2097152 bits (the parser of the reference refuses more).
fn tvtok (u32,u32,bool,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32) u32 (u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32)x128x32 u32 -> (u32,u32,bool,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32,u32)
